{
  "manifest": "efe-mcp-manifest/0",
  "suite": "robocasa-gr1",
  "kind": "rcb",
  "robot": "Fourier GR1 humanoid (arms and waist, fixed in the kitchen) with two six-command Fourier hands; the arms take absolute grip-site pose targets solved by whole-body inverse kinematics",
  "frame": {
    "suite": "the RoboCasa kitchen's world frame (metres, z up)",
    "quat": "wxyz",
    "base": {
      "fixed": [2.65, -2.175, 0.97, 0.707107, 0.0, 0.0, 0.707107]
    },
    "base_text": "the robot base frame (body robot0_base, fixed in the kitchen): +X the way the robot faces, +Y its left, +Z up"
  },
  "cameras": ["robot0_agentview_center", "robot0_agentview_left", "robot0_agentview_right", "egoview", "robot0_eye_in_right_hand", "robot0_eye_in_left_hand"],
  "default_cameras": ["egoview", "robot0_agentview_center"],
  "action_cameras": ["egoview"],
  "state_cameras": ["egoview"],
  "control": {
    "dt": 0.05,
    "control_dt": 0.05,
    "joint_speed": 1.5,
    "min_move_s": 0.5,
    "settle_s": 0.2,
    "tolerance": {
      "joint": 0.05
    }
  },
  "types": {
    "ee_pose": {
      "dim": 24,
      "hold": ["ref"],
      "hold_ref": {
        "names": ["cmd_right_x", "cmd_right_y", "cmd_right_z", "cmd_right_rx", "cmd_right_ry", "cmd_right_rz", "cmd_left_x", "cmd_left_y", "cmd_left_z", "cmd_left_rx", "cmd_left_ry", "cmd_left_rz", "cmd_right_little", "cmd_right_ring", "cmd_right_middle", "cmd_right_index", "cmd_right_thumb_flexion", "cmd_right_thumb_rotation", "cmd_left_little", "cmd_left_ring", "cmd_left_middle", "cmd_left_index", "cmd_left_thumb_flexion", "cmd_left_thumb_rotation"]
      }
    }
  },
  "parts": {
    "right_hand": {
      "kind": "hand",
      "note": "right Fourier hand: six finger position targets (rad) in the order little, ring, middle, index, thumb_flexion, thumb_rotation; 0 = straight and open, about 1.7 = fully bent (closed); values outside 0..1.7 change nothing more",
      "joints": {
        "type": "ee_pose",
        "cols": [12, 18]
      },
      "state": {
        "joints": {
          "names": ["cmd_right_little", "cmd_right_ring", "cmd_right_middle", "cmd_right_index", "cmd_right_thumb_flexion", "cmd_right_thumb_rotation"]
        }
      }
    },
    "left_hand": {
      "kind": "hand",
      "note": "left Fourier hand: six finger position targets (rad) in the order little, ring, middle, index, thumb_flexion, thumb_rotation; 0 = straight and open, about 1.7 = fully bent (closed); values outside 0..1.7 change nothing more",
      "joints": {
        "type": "ee_pose",
        "cols": [18, 24]
      },
      "state": {
        "joints": {
          "names": ["cmd_left_little", "cmd_left_ring", "cmd_left_middle", "cmd_left_index", "cmd_left_thumb_flexion", "cmd_left_thumb_rotation"]
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "notes": "The arms take absolute grip-site pose targets in the robot base frame, sent with execute_trajectory space native, action_type ee_pose (24 numbers, one row per 0.05 s control step, each row a target the whole-body inverse kinematics moves toward): right x, y, z (m), rx, ry, rz (axis-angle, rad), the same for the left, then the six right-hand and six left-hand finger targets. cmd_* in proprio_now is the command in force (start from it and change what should move; interpolate long moves over several rows). The grip site is the origin of the hand's mounting frame at the wrist end of the hand, not a point between the fingertips; the four small pink spheres beside each hand are markers of the robot model. move_robot and execute_trajectory space joint set the fingers (the hands' joint_positions); the reported finger values are the commands in force. eef_left_*/eef_right_* in proprio_now are the grip sites' positions in the world frame. The cameras ride on the robot; each frame comes with its current calibration.",
